'''Rasett Milio ''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[scientist]] who served in the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Tarkin Initiative]] as the [[administrator]] of its [[High Energy Concepts and Implementation Labs|HECIL]] division. Milio's projects focused on the creation of containment channels and [[force field]]s in order to "sheath" energy unleashed by a [[superlaser]] into a [[focusing cone]].<ref name="ROUVG" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Personality and traits==
Rasett Milio had [[hair]] that had turned [[Color|gray]], brown [[eye]]s, and light skin.<ref name="ROUVG" />

==Equipment==
While part of the Kyber crystal research team, Milio wore a blue-and-white [[engineer]]ing [[jumpsuit]].<ref name="Rogue One Novelization">[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (novelization)|''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story'' novelization]]</ref> The jumpsuit had [[Clothing|antiseptic coveralls]], which were marked with the [[Imperial crest|insignia]] of both the Empire and the Tarkin Initiative. His uniform had a tunic that would change colors when in the presence of dangerous [[radiation]], and [[Clothing|shoes]] grounded against potential static charges within the labs. His jumpsuit included a pocket over the chest that held [[code cylinder]]s, which unlocked access to restricted laboratories.<ref name="ROUVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
Rasett Milio first appeared in the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Anthology'']] film, ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'', in which he was portrayed by [[Alan Rushton]]. Though the film's credits refer to him as "Engineer,"<ref name="RO" /> Milio's name was revealed in ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'', a reference book written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]] released on the same day as the film.<ref name="ROUVG" />

